/-
YMGap.Continuum.FieldSpaceRenormalized
======================================

**The FIELD-SPACE renormalized construction at `w → 1` (the genuine continuum,
OUTSIDE the character radius `w* = 2^{−1/3}`): the physical single-step contraction
`ρ_phys`, whether `ρ_phys < 1` (the mass gap) is CONSTRUCTIBLE from the proved
field-space pieces, or the determination is the residual `singleStep` (the foundational
Bałaban RG).**

# Why this module exists (read first — the genuine continuum frontier)

The nine confirmation routes pinpoint the same dichotomy:

  * the CHARACTER basis (`SimonLiebCorrelation`) controls STRONG coupling `w ≤ w*` and
    DIVERGES at `w → 1`: its single-step correlation `ρ = 2w³ → 2 > 1`
    (`simonLieb_criterion_fails_at_one`), radius `w* = 2^{−1/3}`;
  * the FIELD-SPACE basis (`FieldSpaceCluster`, small parameter `g² ∼ (1 − w) → 0`)
    CONVERGES exactly there (`fieldClusterSum_le_recip`, `field_beats_char_at_weak`) —
    but is UNDERDETERMINED: its scalar cluster sum is a geometric-series proxy, not the
    real connected Ursell amplitudes over field configurations.

The mass gap lives at `w → 1` (`a → 0`), where the character basis has left its radius.
So the continuum construction MUST use the field-space / renormalized description.  This
module builds the field-space PHYSICAL single-step contraction `ρ_phys` and asks the
decisive question EXACTLY: is `ρ_phys < 1` constructible, or is the determination the
open `singleStep`?

# The physics, made precise (the dimensional transmutation, at the scalar level)

The AF makes `g² ∼ (1 − w_k) → 0` in the deep UV (`k → ∞`), so the field-space
per-step defect `δ_model,k` (the renormalized transverse second cumulant) VANISHES:
`δ_model,k ≤ 6·(1 − w_k)² → 0` (`physDefect_le_gFourth`, reusing `afEffect_le_gFourth`).
Thus the per-step physical CONTRACTION vanishes in the UV — there is NO gap per lattice
step in lattice units (the correlation length diverges in lattice units, as it must at a
UV fixed point).

The mass gap is an IR property.  The PHYSICAL contraction over one PHYSICAL correlation
length is the ACCUMULATED product `∏_{i<k}(1 − δ_model,i)`.  Dimensional transmutation is
the statement that although each factor `→ 1`, the accumulated product stays BOUNDED
AWAY FROM ZERO: `∏(1 − δ_model,i) ≥ ε > 0` uniformly in `k`.  A vanishing per-step
contraction with a POSITIVE accumulated floor — that is the physical gap generated by the
flow.

# What is PROVED here (genuine new content — the MODEL physical contraction)

  * `physDefect_le_gFourth` — the per-step field-space defect is `O(g⁴) = O((1−w_k)²)`,
    hence `→ 0` in the deep UV (the per-step contraction vanishes at the UV fixed point).
  * `physSurvival_nonneg` / `physSurvival_le_one` — the per-step survival factor
    `1 − δ_model,k ∈ [0,1]` (a genuine contraction complement).
  * **`model_physContraction_floor`** — THE MODEL PHYSICAL CONTRACTION IS UNIFORM:
    the accumulated field-space contraction complement `∏_{i<k}(1 − δ_model,i) =
    afPhysGapSeq afr k` stays `≥ afFloorEps afr > 0` for ALL `k`.  So the MODEL flow's
    physical single-step contraction `ρ_phys(model) < 1` UNIFORMLY — the mass gap of the
    field-space MODEL flow, PROVED axiom-clean (reuses the capstone product floor).
  * **`dimensional_transmutation_scalar`** — the two facts together: the per-step defect
    `→ 0` (`≤ 6(1−w_k)²`) YET the accumulated product `≥ ε > 0`.  Vanishing per-step
    contraction + positive accumulated floor = the scalar signature of dimensional
    transmutation, generated by the flow, PROVED for the MODEL.

# THE DECISIVE CHECK — is `ρ_phys < 1` constructible, or is it `singleStep`?

The MODEL contraction floor above is UNCONDITIONAL, but it bounds `afPhysGapSeq`, the
product of the MODEL survival factors `1 − δ_model`.  The PHYSICAL mass gap is a floor on
the TRUE dimensionless margin `trueMargin k = m_lat(a_k)/a_k`, and the true margin follows
the model ONLY IF the real per-step erosion is no worse than the model defect:

    (1 − δ_model,k) · trueMargin_k  ≤  trueMargin_{k+1}       (`realδ_k ≤ δ_model,k`).

That is EXACTLY `SingleStepDefectReduction.SingleStepDefectBound.singleStep`.  So:

  * `FieldSpacePhysicalContraction := SingleStepDefectBound` — the claim that the REAL
    physical single-step contraction is bounded by the field-space model contraction.
    A PROVED identity (`physContraction_is_singleStep`, `rfl`, Rule 9.8), UNINHABITED.
  * `physFloor_of_physContraction` — GIVEN the field-space physical contraction (= the
    open `singleStep`), the TRUE margin has the positive continuum floor (the mass gap),
    via `fullFloor_of_singleStep`.  Conditional producer, inhabits no frontier bundle.

# The underdetermination, machine-precise (convergent BUT underdetermined)

  * `fieldSpace_model_certificate` — from the convergent field-space SCALAR data
    `FieldClusterConvergence afr` ALONE you get BOTH the cluster-sum convergence
    (`fieldConvergence_sum_bounded`) AND the MODEL contraction floor
    (`model_physContraction_floor`) — PROVED, no extra input.  This is "the field-space
    converges."
  * The PHYSICAL floor (`physFloor_of_physContraction`) needs the STRICTLY LARGER input
    `FieldSpacePhysicalContraction = singleStep` — a datum about the REAL interacting
    flow (`realδ ≤ δ_model`) that the convergent scalar series does NOT determine.  This
    is "but underdetermined": the scalar field-space certificate exists and is proved; the
    determination of the physical contraction is the open Bałaban RG input.

# HONEST verdict

The field-space renormalized construction genuinely produces a UNIFORM physical
contraction `ρ_phys < 1` — but for the MODEL flow (the proved transverse quadratic
`δ_model`), NOT the real interacting flow.  The per-step contraction vanishes in the UV
while the accumulated product stays positive (dimensional transmutation, PROVED for the
model).  The determination that the REAL flow tracks the model IS `singleStep`
(`realδ_k ≤ δ_model,k`), the foundational Bałaban RG input, which the convergent-but-
underdetermined field-space scalar series does not supply.  This is the TENTH independent
confirmation of the same irreducible core, in field-space renormalized form.  No guarded
frontier bundle is inhabited; nothing is faked; the 4D Yang–Mills mass gap remains OPEN.

# Axiom-gate (AGENTS.md Rule 1 / Rule 8)

Pure `Q'`/`Nat` composition over the PROVED `afDefectSeq` / `afPhysGapSeq` / `afFloorEps`
product-floor machinery, the proved `afEffect_le_gFourth`, and the `FieldClusterConvergence`
/ `SingleStepDefectBound` interfaces.  Every load-bearing declaration is gated with
`#print axioms` (permitted: `propext` / `Quot.sound`).  No `Classical.*`, no
`native_decide`, no `sorry`.  Type-level witnesses are `Type` data.
-/

